WEBVTT

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.651
Doctor?

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.586
Oh, hello, Quark.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:22.645
Oh...

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:24.316
Let me guess...

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.985
eavesdropping
on the battling O'Briens.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.619
Don't be ridiculous.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.993
Such language.

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:33.693
Oh, I hope Molly's not around.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:36.327
You can hear what they're
saying in there?

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.996
How could I not?

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.471
Well, what are they saying?

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:43.670
Let's use a little discretion,
shall we?

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.772
He's done something.

00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:50.510
She's outraged.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.518
He thinks she's overreacting.

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.850
She thinks he's trying
to run her life.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.879
Pretty boring, actually...

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.025
but to hear them

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.460
you'd think it was a matter
of life and death.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.395
Hello, Julian.

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:07.360
Hello.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:08.958
Quark.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.300
Mrs. O'Brien.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:14.272
I thought you said the O'Briens
were arguing in there.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:16.138
Not Miles and Keiko...

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:19.475
the other O'Briens,
Miles and Kira.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.480
What do they have
to argue about?

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.607
Miles hid Kira's
springball racket

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.618
because she's carrying his baby

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:28.143
and he doesn't want her
taking any risks

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:30.816
and she doesn't want him
controlling her...

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:34.493
What?

00:01:34.527 --> 00:01:36.324
Keiko made them stop.

00:01:36.362 --> 00:01:39.991
Now they're in the "let's talk
this out and share our feelings"

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.330
part of the fight.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.995
Show's over.

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:47.200
Oh, well.
I mean, good.

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.798
It is the power of his voice

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.537
the strength of his intonation

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:52.636
that make Barak-Kadan
a great singer.

00:01:52.679 --> 00:01:54.340
There are none like him.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.847
None as boring anyway.

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:57.941
He never varies his performance

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.576
not even by a half-tone.

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.883
I prefer traditional
opera performed

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.513
in the traditional manner.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:06.525
You know, for a Klingon
who was raised by humans

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:08.117
wears a Starfleet uniform

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:10.254
and drinks prune juice

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.491
you're pretty attached
to tradition.

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:14.523
But that's okay.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:17.161
I like a man riddled
with contradictions.

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:30.607
That's a welcome sight.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:32.618
The peace talks
must be going well

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.984
if the Klingons are
back on the station.

00:02:35.021 --> 00:02:36.318
Worf?

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.388
Did you see her?

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.952
The Klingon woman?

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:47.728
She was glorious.

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:05.951
Her?

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.646
She's okay.

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.254
I have never seen such a woman.

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:14.954
Who is she?
What House is she from?

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:19.397
I do not recognize
her family crest.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:41.448
She is a friend of the Ferengi.

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.319
Now I remember who she is.

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:48.987
Her name is Grilka.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:52.156
And she's not just
Quark's friend...

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:54.359
she's his ex-wife.

00:05:58.424 --> 00:05:59.755
Maporian ale

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:02.022
with just a hint
of pazafer as I recall.

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:04.029
You remember.
I'm honored.

00:06:04.063 --> 00:06:05.121
How could I forget?

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:06.825
You're the only Klingon I know

00:06:06.865 --> 00:06:09.197
who drinks something
besides bloodwine...

00:06:09.234 --> 00:06:10.201
or prune juice.

00:06:10.235 --> 00:06:12.032
Prune juice?

00:06:12.071 --> 00:06:13.936
Forget it.

00:06:14.039 --> 00:06:15.700
To the House of Grilka.

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:18.539
May it continue to be
as strong and as proud

00:06:18.577 --> 00:06:20.511
as its lady is beautiful.

00:06:26.151 --> 00:06:28.711
You may not have been
the ideal husband

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:30.619
but you are
an excellent bartender.

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:32.647
I know of no greater compliment.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.491
So...

00:06:36.528 --> 00:06:39.691
what brings you
to my humble establishment?

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:41.393
Business or pleasure?

00:06:47.206 --> 00:06:50.664
The recent hostilities between
the Federation and the Empire

00:06:50.709 --> 00:06:53.837
have been very costly
to my family.

00:06:53.879 --> 00:06:58.816
We have suffered great losses
in ships, lands, warriors.

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:00.751
War... what is it good for?

00:07:00.786 --> 00:07:03.254
If you ask me,
absolutely nothing.

00:07:03.288 --> 00:07:07.315
The financial cost
was significant.

00:07:07.359 --> 00:07:08.917
I have an idea.

00:07:08.994 --> 00:07:12.725
Why don't I take a look
at your financial records?

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:15.029
I know that's not
why you're here.

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:17.467
I'm sure it's simply
a social visit

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:18.902
but maybe I could help.

00:07:18.937 --> 00:07:21.804
Very well.

00:07:21.840 --> 00:07:27.403
If it pleases you, I will
allow you access to the records.

00:07:27.446 --> 00:07:29.277
Thank you.

00:07:35.354 --> 00:07:37.652
Hear this, Ferengi.

00:07:37.689 --> 00:07:41.955
Help Grilka and you live.

00:07:42.027 --> 00:07:43.654
Fail...

00:07:43.695 --> 00:07:47.899
and I will kill you myself.

00:07:50.067 --> 00:07:52.160
And even though
it was an accident

00:07:52.203 --> 00:07:55.400
Quark took credit
for killing Grilka's husband.

00:07:55.439 --> 00:07:56.565
Why?

00:07:56.607 --> 00:07:58.871
As a way of boosting
business at the bar.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:00.241
And it worked.

00:08:00.278 --> 00:08:01.870
But then Grilka kidnapped Quark

00:08:01.913 --> 00:08:04.177
and took him back
to the Klingon Homeworld

00:08:04.215 --> 00:08:05.182
and married him.

00:08:05.216 --> 00:08:06.615
Why?

00:08:06.651 --> 00:08:08.482
I'm getting to that.

00:08:08.519 --> 00:08:13.286
As a woman, Grilka was forbidden
to lead her House.

00:08:13.324 --> 00:08:16.725
By marrying Quark, she could
retain control through him.

00:08:16.761 --> 00:08:20.697
Eventually, she convinced
the Council to give her control

00:08:20.731 --> 00:08:22.926
and she divorced Quark
on the spot.

00:08:22.967 --> 00:08:24.264
As far as I know

00:08:24.302 --> 00:08:26.566
that's the last time
they saw each other.

00:08:26.604 --> 00:08:28.799
A marriage of convenience.

00:08:28.839 --> 00:08:30.932
Certainly for Grilka,
but I'm not sure

00:08:31.008 --> 00:08:32.805
how convenient it was for Quark.

00:08:32.843 --> 00:08:35.243
His opinion is
of no consequence.

00:08:35.279 --> 00:08:38.715
He is unworthy
of such a prize as she.

00:08:38.749 --> 00:08:44.483
Worf, it sounds like you have
a bad case of par'Mach.

00:08:44.522 --> 00:08:46.513
Is that contagious?

00:08:49.694 --> 00:08:52.959
Par'Mach is the
Klingon word for love

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:55.498
but with more
aggressive overtones.

00:08:55.533 --> 00:08:56.830
Love?

00:08:56.867 --> 00:08:57.891
Worf?

00:08:59.337 --> 00:09:02.272
Stranger things have happened.

00:09:02.306 --> 00:09:04.297
Especially around here.

00:09:09.747 --> 00:09:12.341
This should alleviate
Kira's sneezing.

00:09:12.383 --> 00:09:13.816
Should?

00:09:13.851 --> 00:09:15.682
Bajoran women
have been sneezing

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:18.621
their way through pregnancy
for over 100,000 years.

00:09:18.656 --> 00:09:21.318
You can't expect me
to cure it overnight.

00:09:24.328 --> 00:09:27.388
You know, I heard a rumor
that the Jerries might be trying

00:09:27.431 --> 00:09:29.296
to cross the Channel
this evening.

00:09:29.333 --> 00:09:32.325
Maybe we should have a surprise
waiting for them.

00:09:33.671 --> 00:09:36.299
Serves you right.

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:38.672
I can't go
to the holosuite tonight.

00:09:38.709 --> 00:09:41.200
Kira and I have some things
to work out.

00:09:41.245 --> 00:09:44.146
Still fighting, eh?

00:09:44.181 --> 00:09:45.580
Who says we're fighting?

00:09:45.616 --> 00:09:46.947
Well, word gets around.

00:09:47.018 --> 00:09:48.781
It's a small station.

00:09:48.819 --> 00:09:50.309
It's a huge station.

00:09:50.354 --> 00:09:53.323
Obviously not huge enough.

00:09:53.357 --> 00:09:56.292
Well, for your information,
we are not fighting.

00:09:56.327 --> 00:09:57.726
Glad to hear it.

00:09:57.762 --> 00:10:00.663
Bajoran takeo herbs
for Kira's swollen ankles.

00:10:00.698 --> 00:10:02.290
She'll need to dissolve them

00:10:02.333 --> 00:10:05.166
in some kind of fruit juice
before ingesting them.

00:10:05.202 --> 00:10:06.464
I hope they taste better

00:10:06.504 --> 00:10:08.529
than those makora
herbs you gave her.

00:10:08.572 --> 00:10:11.769
Are you sampling
all her medications?

00:10:11.809 --> 00:10:15.609
No...
Kira didn't like the taste.

00:10:15.646 --> 00:10:17.807
Oh, by the way, I almost forgot.

00:10:17.848 --> 00:10:19.679
She, uh...

00:10:19.717 --> 00:10:23.744
she has a... a rash
on the back of her thighs.

00:10:23.788 --> 00:10:25.585
Do you have a salve
or something?

00:10:25.623 --> 00:10:27.523
How long has she had it?

00:10:27.558 --> 00:10:28.616
Well, I noticed it yesterday

00:10:28.659 --> 00:10:30.524
when I was helping her out
of the bathtub

00:10:30.561 --> 00:10:32.222
so she's had it at least a day.

00:10:32.263 --> 00:10:34.254
Helping her out of the tub?

00:10:34.298 --> 00:10:35.822
She's living in my house.

00:10:35.866 --> 00:10:37.163
She's having my baby.

00:10:37.201 --> 00:10:40.329
So, uh, did you look?

00:10:40.371 --> 00:10:41.531
What?

00:10:41.572 --> 00:10:44.370
Oh, please.

00:10:44.408 --> 00:10:47.138
I was holding a towel up
in front of her.

00:10:47.178 --> 00:10:52.445
How does Keiko feel about you
helping Kira out of the tub?

00:10:52.483 --> 00:10:54.417
Keiko feels fine about it.

00:10:54.452 --> 00:10:56.010
You see, we are adults.

00:10:56.053 --> 00:10:58.988
We've developed
a close, mature relationship.

00:10:59.023 --> 00:11:01.389
I'm sure
that Keiko and Kira have

00:11:01.425 --> 00:11:02.949
but you...

00:11:03.027 --> 00:11:04.790
What about me?

00:11:04.829 --> 00:11:07.354
I'll bet you looked.

00:11:35.392 --> 00:11:38.850
I will apologize for this
at a later time.

00:11:38.896 --> 00:11:41.387
You are in my seat!

00:11:44.068 --> 00:11:45.535
Bartender!

00:11:45.569 --> 00:11:47.560
Bloodwine!

00:11:51.408 --> 00:11:55.003
What is that smell?

00:11:55.079 --> 00:11:58.674
Is there a pile
of rotting forshak in here?

00:12:01.085 --> 00:12:04.316
Or is it you?

00:12:07.258 --> 00:12:09.453
Stand when I talk to you!

00:12:11.095 --> 00:12:12.892
Or do you think it is funny?

00:12:12.930 --> 00:12:14.295
Mev yap!

00:12:17.902 --> 00:12:20.666
Worf, son of Mogh.

00:12:20.704 --> 00:12:23.366
Come. Join me.

00:12:28.712 --> 00:12:33.513
Challenging Thopok to a fight
is a waste of time.

00:12:33.551 --> 00:12:36.748
Grilka cannot mate with you,
now or ever.

00:12:36.787 --> 00:12:39.347
Your House is dishonored.

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:41.187
Your name is a curse.

00:12:41.225 --> 00:12:42.852
I meant no disrespect.

00:12:42.893 --> 00:12:44.724
You showed none.

00:12:44.762 --> 00:12:47.390
I'm sure your motives
were honorable.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:51.862
Do not let it
trouble you too much.

00:12:51.902 --> 00:12:55.030
In truth, I doubt it would
have been a good match.

00:12:56.407 --> 00:12:57.874
Why?

00:12:59.076 --> 00:13:02.512
Have you ever pursued
a Klingon woman?

00:13:04.515 --> 00:13:05.573
No.

00:13:05.616 --> 00:13:07.413
There's no shame in that.

00:13:07.451 --> 00:13:08.918
You were raised by humans.

00:13:08.953 --> 00:13:10.352
You wear their uniform.

00:13:10.387 --> 00:13:12.685
You accept their values.

00:13:12.723 --> 00:13:15.385
How could you know anything
about our women?

00:13:15.426 --> 00:13:18.156
You'd be surprised what I know.

00:13:18.195 --> 00:13:19.526
Perhaps.

00:13:19.563 --> 00:13:21.827
But we will not find out here.

00:13:21.865 --> 00:13:24.459
It is the wish
of the Lady Grilka

00:13:24.501 --> 00:13:27.664
that you leave us now,
son of Mogh

00:13:27.705 --> 00:13:30.105
and do not return.

00:13:47.524 --> 00:13:49.958
I am a fool.

00:13:49.994 --> 00:13:52.326
You're in love.

00:13:52.363 --> 00:13:54.729
Which I suppose
is the same thing.

00:13:54.765 --> 00:13:57.290
You're making
too much of this, Worf.

00:13:57.334 --> 00:13:59.700
Tumek said that Grilka
wasn't offended.

00:13:59.737 --> 00:14:01.466
She was probably flattered.

00:14:01.505 --> 00:14:02.938
There is no flattery

00:14:03.007 --> 00:14:05.339
in a great lady
being courted by a traitor.

00:14:09.179 --> 00:14:11.613
Is that what's really
bothering you?

00:14:11.649 --> 00:14:13.947
Or is it that Tumek said
that you didn't know

00:14:14.051 --> 00:14:15.678
anything about Klingon women

00:14:15.719 --> 00:14:17.448
and you're afraid he's right?

00:14:20.491 --> 00:14:22.652
What do you want?

00:14:22.693 --> 00:14:25.526
I want to talk to Dax
if that's all right with you.

00:14:31.268 --> 00:14:32.565
I need help.

00:14:32.603 --> 00:14:34.969
Grilka invited me to dinner

00:14:35.039 --> 00:14:39.408
and I need to brush up
on Klingon manners and protocol.

00:14:39.443 --> 00:14:40.501
She invited you to dinner?

00:14:40.544 --> 00:14:42.068
In her quarters.

00:14:42.112 --> 00:14:43.739
A private dinner.

00:14:43.781 --> 00:14:45.544
A very private dinner.

00:14:48.419 --> 00:14:50.614
What's wrong with him?

00:14:50.654 --> 00:14:52.485
He's having a bad day.

00:14:52.523 --> 00:14:54.684
Oh, that's a shame.

00:14:54.725 --> 00:14:58.821
Well, when Grilka and I
were married

00:14:58.862 --> 00:15:02.059
there wasn't a lot of, um...

00:15:02.099 --> 00:15:03.532
affection involved.

00:15:03.567 --> 00:15:06.229
So, what does a Klingon woman
expect from a man?

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:09.103
Are there any secret
Klingon phrases I should know

00:15:09.139 --> 00:15:12.597
or do we just leap on each other
like a pair of crazed voles?

00:15:12.643 --> 00:15:19.572
Quark, Klingon mating rituals
are very... involved.

00:15:19.616 --> 00:15:21.277
It's not just
a one-night affair.

00:15:21.318 --> 00:15:22.307
Two nights.

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:24.509
Whatever.

00:15:24.555 --> 00:15:27.683
Look, I'm serious.

00:15:27.725 --> 00:15:32.458
Grilka and I, we have
something...

00:15:32.496 --> 00:15:34.964
I'm not sure what.

00:15:35.065 --> 00:15:36.532
But I want to pursue it.

00:15:36.567 --> 00:15:37.591
For sex?

00:15:37.634 --> 00:15:40.967
No!
Well, yeah, that, too.

00:15:41.004 --> 00:15:43.768
But there's more.

00:15:43.807 --> 00:15:45.642
She's glorious.

00:15:46.876 --> 00:15:48.207
So I hear.

00:15:49.846 --> 00:15:53.247
Look... if you're serious
about this

00:15:53.282 --> 00:15:55.443
then you have to take it
slow at dinner.

00:15:55.485 --> 00:15:57.146
No innuendoes.

00:15:57.186 --> 00:15:59.518
No staring at her cleavage.

00:16:01.290 --> 00:16:03.155
So what do I do?

00:16:03.192 --> 00:16:04.523
You talk.

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:06.721
You ask her
about her family's history

00:16:06.763 --> 00:16:08.287
and their accomplishments.

00:16:08.331 --> 00:16:10.856
She'll consider this
a great sign of respect.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:13.027
Respect?

00:16:13.069 --> 00:16:14.730
Okay, okay.

00:16:14.771 --> 00:16:16.068
I can do that.

00:16:16.105 --> 00:16:17.595
Anything else?

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:19.938
Grilka is
from the Mekro'vak region.

00:16:20.043 --> 00:16:22.204
It is customary among her people

00:16:22.245 --> 00:16:24.736
that the man bring
the leg of a lingta

00:16:24.781 --> 00:16:26.806
to the first courtship dinner.

00:16:26.849 --> 00:16:29.818
Make sure it's fresh,
as if you have just killed it.

00:16:29.852 --> 00:16:32.719
Then use the leg to sweep aside
everything on the table

00:16:32.755 --> 00:16:35.849
and declare in a loud voice,
"I have brought you this!

00:16:35.892 --> 00:16:36.859
"From this day,

00:16:36.893 --> 00:16:39.157
"I wish to provide food
for you and your House.

00:16:39.195 --> 00:16:41.595
"All I ask
is to share your company

00:16:41.631 --> 00:16:43.531
and do honor to your name."

00:16:43.566 --> 00:16:46.933
Then what?

00:16:46.969 --> 00:16:51.599
Well, either she accepts
your offer...

00:16:51.641 --> 00:16:53.973
or she has her bodyguard

00:16:54.043 --> 00:16:55.806
shatter every bone
in your body.

00:17:00.316 --> 00:17:01.613
Sounds reasonable.

00:17:11.961 --> 00:17:14.589
So did your father
just sit you down one day

00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:16.359
and say, "All right, Miles.

00:17:16.399 --> 00:17:17.661
"It's time to teach you

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:19.463
about massaging
pregnant women"?

00:17:19.502 --> 00:17:21.936
It's an O'Brien
survival technique.

00:17:22.038 --> 00:17:24.029
My mother hated being pregnant.

00:17:24.073 --> 00:17:25.938
My father's massages
were the only things

00:17:25.975 --> 00:17:27.602
that kept her
from killing everyone.

00:17:27.643 --> 00:17:29.076
Sounds like me.

00:17:29.112 --> 00:17:30.374
Pretty much.

00:17:30.413 --> 00:17:31.937
She didn't swear in Bajoran

00:17:32.048 --> 00:17:33.709
but she did like to use

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:36.344
what she called
"descriptive phrases."

00:17:39.689 --> 00:17:41.213
Are those my uniforms?

00:17:41.257 --> 00:17:43.657
Garak finished the alterations
and...

00:17:43.693 --> 00:17:45.058
he sent these along.

00:17:45.094 --> 00:17:47.654
He guarantees
the insoles will help your feet.

00:17:47.697 --> 00:17:48.891
Ow, ow...
ow!

00:17:48.931 --> 00:17:51.161
That wasn't
very convincing.

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:53.361
I think she's actually
enjoying it, Miles.

00:17:53.402 --> 00:17:55.927
You better press harder
if you want her to suffer.

00:17:55.972 --> 00:17:58.532
Harder, it is.

00:17:58.574 --> 00:18:00.599
Ow, ooh!

00:18:00.643 --> 00:18:03.908
You are a sadist,
Miles Edward O'Brien.

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:06.278
Was your father
this cruel to your mother?

00:18:06.315 --> 00:18:09.182
Worse. I'd swear sometimes
you'd hear her screams

00:18:09.218 --> 00:18:10.617
halfway across Ireland.

00:18:10.653 --> 00:18:12.120
The neighbors didn't know

00:18:12.155 --> 00:18:14.282
whether to be worried
or titillated.

00:18:15.758 --> 00:18:17.749
Oh...

00:18:17.794 --> 00:18:20.024
here.

00:18:23.733 --> 00:18:25.633
You miss Ireland?

00:18:25.668 --> 00:18:28.364
You know, if you'd
asked me that a year ago

00:18:28.404 --> 00:18:29.928
I would have said no

00:18:30.006 --> 00:18:33.669
but lately,
and I don't know why

00:18:33.709 --> 00:18:36.473
I've been daydreaming
about home.

00:18:36.512 --> 00:18:40.107
Maybe I'm getting
nostalgic in my old age.

00:18:40.149 --> 00:18:41.810
Mmm.

00:18:41.851 --> 00:18:43.944
You've got leave coming.

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:46.045
Take three weeks and go.

00:18:46.088 --> 00:18:49.819
If I left,
who'd give you foot massages?

00:18:49.859 --> 00:18:51.121
Take me along.

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:53.128
I can think of worse things

00:18:53.162 --> 00:18:56.461
than spending
three weeks in Ireland with you.

00:18:56.499 --> 00:18:58.262
Me, too.

00:19:06.776 --> 00:19:09.006
Don't stop on my account.

00:19:09.045 --> 00:19:10.945
Oh, right.

00:19:19.322 --> 00:19:25.090
BOW-cha-daay

00:19:25.127 --> 00:19:33.432
KEY-cha-day

00:19:33.469 --> 00:19:41.535
Me-Yo-ca-BEEN-eva-kaa-MOR

00:19:41.577 --> 00:19:47.243
LING-tomaH

00:19:47.283 --> 00:19:52.778
oH-ma-do-VEE-kos ZO!

00:19:52.822 --> 00:19:55.313
OH-ma-do-VEE-kos ZO...

00:20:00.997 --> 00:20:02.965
I'm not going to ask.

00:20:03.032 --> 00:20:06.433
Look, I came here
to thank you for last night.

00:20:06.469 --> 00:20:09.461
Grilka loved it... all of it...
everything I did.

00:20:09.505 --> 00:20:13.202
Everything I said was perfect.

00:20:13.242 --> 00:20:15.836
So, I know nothing
about Klingon women.

00:20:15.878 --> 00:20:18.642
She said I had the heart
of a Basai Master...

00:20:18.681 --> 00:20:19.841
whatever that is.

00:20:19.882 --> 00:20:21.144
It is a poet.

00:20:21.183 --> 00:20:23.344
A poet?

00:20:23.386 --> 00:20:25.877
I guess I can live with that.

00:20:27.590 --> 00:20:29.080
What else happened?

00:20:29.125 --> 00:20:30.888
She spent about an hour

00:20:30.927 --> 00:20:32.986
talking about her
family history...

00:20:33.029 --> 00:20:35.725
a rather long and bloody tale

00:20:35.765 --> 00:20:38.393
but what else is new?

00:20:38.434 --> 00:20:42.530
Then, we ate the lingta...

00:20:42.571 --> 00:20:45.836
which tasted really bad...

00:20:45.875 --> 00:20:47.365
listened to some noise

00:20:47.410 --> 00:20:49.469
which she called
Klingon music

00:20:49.512 --> 00:20:51.605
and then I left.

00:20:51.647 --> 00:20:53.012
A perfect evening.

00:20:53.049 --> 00:20:54.209
Mmm.

00:20:55.651 --> 00:20:57.016
Almost.

00:20:57.053 --> 00:21:00.113
Her bodyguard was giving me
threatening looks all night.

00:21:00.156 --> 00:21:01.646
That is to be expected.

00:21:01.691 --> 00:21:05.092
The idea of a Ferengi
courting a great lady is...

00:21:05.127 --> 00:21:06.560
offensive.

00:21:06.595 --> 00:21:07.960
You know,
it's attitudes like that

00:21:08.064 --> 00:21:09.497
that keep you people
from getting invited

00:21:09.532 --> 00:21:11.295
to all the really good parties.

00:21:11.334 --> 00:21:12.961
"The heart of a Basai Master..."

00:21:13.002 --> 00:21:14.230
She said that?

00:21:14.270 --> 00:21:16.295
Could I make that up?

00:21:19.141 --> 00:21:23.373
I'm telling you, Worf,
she responded perfectly.

00:21:24.613 --> 00:21:28.140
You really have the key
to this woman's heart.

00:21:28.184 --> 00:21:29.549
The question is:

00:21:29.585 --> 00:21:31.644
Can you help me unlock it?

00:21:35.624 --> 00:21:37.615
Yes, I can.

00:21:38.894 --> 00:21:40.691
We have work to do.

00:22:15.264 --> 00:22:16.322
Quark.

00:22:24.774 --> 00:22:27.800
MoVas ah-kee rustak!

00:22:30.346 --> 00:22:32.871
Kosh tomaH.

00:22:32.915 --> 00:22:34.644
Kosh tomoh...

00:22:34.683 --> 00:22:39.746
I mean,
tomaH ehpaq Lukara kaVeir.

00:22:39.789 --> 00:22:43.486
Ish-tovee chuCH thling nuq?

00:22:43.526 --> 00:22:44.823
Besh...

00:22:44.860 --> 00:22:48.091
besh-opar gree urch...

00:22:49.498 --> 00:22:51.398
Besh...

00:22:51.434 --> 00:22:58.738
opar gee urchun
tomaH te... te...

00:22:58.774 --> 00:23:01.038
te-doQ maugh-shta.

00:23:01.077 --> 00:23:02.476
Enough.

00:23:03.646 --> 00:23:06.171
You say the words,
but there is no feeling

00:23:06.215 --> 00:23:07.443
behind them... no passion.

00:23:07.483 --> 00:23:09.417
Having to learn
all this Klingonese

00:23:09.452 --> 00:23:11.113
isn't helping my performance.

00:23:11.153 --> 00:23:12.518
Do not think of it
as a performance.

00:23:12.555 --> 00:23:14.250
Believe in where you are.

00:23:14.290 --> 00:23:17.817
Put yourself in this place,
in this time...

00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:22.854
a thousand years ago,
the dawn of the Empire.

00:23:22.898 --> 00:23:27.062
500 warriors stormed the
Great Hall at Qam-Chee.

00:23:27.103 --> 00:23:30.266
The city garrison
fled before them.

00:23:30.306 --> 00:23:33.503
Only the Emperor Kahless
and the Lady Lukara

00:23:33.542 --> 00:23:34.975
stood their ground.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:37.069
It was here that they began

00:23:37.113 --> 00:23:40.139
the greatest romance
in Klingon history.

00:23:40.182 --> 00:23:41.979
This is ridiculous.

00:23:42.017 --> 00:23:43.314
Ah!

00:23:43.352 --> 00:23:45.980
I'm surrounded by corpses.

00:23:46.088 --> 00:23:48.322
My shoes are dripping in blood

00:23:48.455 --> 00:23:50.923
and you want me
to feel romantic?

00:23:52.359 --> 00:23:54.987
Why am I putting myself
through this?

00:23:55.062 --> 00:23:57.929
Because later that night,
Kahless and Lukara

00:23:57.964 --> 00:24:02.196
jumped on each other
like a pair of crazed voles.

00:24:03.737 --> 00:24:05.534
Yeah?

00:24:05.572 --> 00:24:07.301
One more time.

00:24:10.544 --> 00:24:11.943
This is the fourth theft
of equipment

00:24:11.978 --> 00:24:13.946
from Upper Pylon 3 this month.

00:24:14.014 --> 00:24:15.641
I don't know how
they keep doing it.

00:24:15.682 --> 00:24:18.412
We've changed the security
protocols three times now.

00:24:18.452 --> 00:24:20.784
It's not
the security arrangements

00:24:20.821 --> 00:24:22.118
that are at fault here.

00:24:22.155 --> 00:24:24.487
It's our friend,
the Chief of Operations.

00:24:24.524 --> 00:24:26.355
Miles?
What did he do?

00:24:26.393 --> 00:24:27.883
It's what he's not doing.

00:24:27.928 --> 00:24:29.225
He still hasn't finished

00:24:29.262 --> 00:24:31.389
upgrading the structural
integrity field

00:24:31.431 --> 00:24:32.728
on Upper Pylon 3.

00:24:32.766 --> 00:24:34.631
So half the bulkheads
are torn open.

00:24:34.668 --> 00:24:37.262
A child could find a way
into those cargo bays.

00:24:37.304 --> 00:24:39.864
Look, Miles is a very busy man,
he can't be everywhere at once.

00:24:39.906 --> 00:24:43.433
Sometimes it seems as though
he's not anywhere at all.

00:24:43.477 --> 00:24:47.208
He is doing a superb job under
very difficult circumstances.

00:24:48.415 --> 00:24:50.315
Ah...

00:24:50.350 --> 00:24:52.841
Growing fond of the Chief,
are we?

00:24:52.886 --> 00:24:54.683
What are you talking about?

00:24:54.721 --> 00:24:56.188
I've always liked Miles.

00:24:56.223 --> 00:24:59.556
You've always liked the Chief

00:24:59.593 --> 00:25:03.927
but Miles
is a different story.

00:25:03.997 --> 00:25:05.191
Look, I...

00:25:05.232 --> 00:25:06.631
I am living with him.

00:25:06.666 --> 00:25:08.133
I am carrying his baby.

00:25:08.168 --> 00:25:10.693
Don't you think that
might change things a bit?

00:25:10.737 --> 00:25:13.433
How so?

00:25:13.473 --> 00:25:15.202
We're closer.

00:25:15.242 --> 00:25:17.870
It-it's like I'm part
of his family.

00:25:20.847 --> 00:25:23.145
Which part?

00:25:23.183 --> 00:25:24.480
What?

00:25:24.518 --> 00:25:26.850
Which part
of his family are you?

00:25:26.887 --> 00:25:30.482
Sister? Daughter? Cousin?

00:25:30.524 --> 00:25:34.585
Could we concentrate on
the criminal activities report?

00:25:34.628 --> 00:25:36.255
Of course.

00:25:36.296 --> 00:25:40.232
And I'll refrain from making
any further disparaging remarks

00:25:40.267 --> 00:25:42.565
about the Chief.

00:25:42.602 --> 00:25:45.366
I mean, Miles.

00:26:00.053 --> 00:26:03.352
This consorting with a...
Ferengi

00:26:03.390 --> 00:26:04.687
is outrageous!

00:26:04.724 --> 00:26:06.521
You forget yourself,
Thopok.

00:26:06.560 --> 00:26:09.188
You are the Commander
of the Lady's Guard

00:26:09.229 --> 00:26:10.355
nothing more.

00:26:10.397 --> 00:26:12.763
Do not presume to judge her.

00:26:20.407 --> 00:26:23.843
Tumek, Maporian ale for two.

00:26:23.877 --> 00:26:25.242
Mistress.

00:26:25.278 --> 00:26:28.543
You are an interesting man.

00:26:28.582 --> 00:26:29.879
I always thought so.

00:26:29.916 --> 00:26:31.747
Not much of a fighter,
of course.

00:26:31.785 --> 00:26:35.186
Fortunately for you,
they were only holo-warriors.

00:26:35.222 --> 00:26:37.713
Well, it's the thought
that counts.

00:26:37.757 --> 00:26:39.224
Yes, it is.

00:26:39.259 --> 00:26:42.057
And what are your thoughts,
Quark?

00:26:42.095 --> 00:26:45.189
Why play out one of
the most romantic scenes

00:26:45.232 --> 00:26:47.496
in Klingon literature for me?

00:26:47.534 --> 00:26:52.403
Why learn to speak Klingon
and observe our customs?

00:26:55.041 --> 00:26:57.635
Why do you pursue me?

00:26:57.677 --> 00:27:01.135
I only pursue those things
I wish to acquire.

00:27:01.181 --> 00:27:03.672
"Acquire"?

00:27:03.717 --> 00:27:07.517
Now you sound like
a Ferengi again.

00:27:07.554 --> 00:27:08.851
I am a Ferengi.

00:27:08.889 --> 00:27:10.516
That means I have a talent

00:27:10.557 --> 00:27:12.855
for appreciating objects
of great value.

00:27:12.893 --> 00:27:14.861
And I believe

00:27:14.895 --> 00:27:19.059
you may be worth more than
all the latinum in the Quadrant.

00:27:26.740 --> 00:27:28.765
My Kahless.

00:27:31.244 --> 00:27:32.768
My Lukara.

00:27:36.383 --> 00:27:38.146
Mev yap, Thopok!

00:27:38.184 --> 00:27:39.481
Forgive me, Mistress

00:27:39.519 --> 00:27:41.350
but I cannot watch
this any longer.

00:27:41.388 --> 00:27:44.721
I will not protect a House
where you are welcome, Ferengi.

00:27:44.758 --> 00:27:46.191
You are a coward

00:27:46.226 --> 00:27:48.251
and a liar

00:27:48.295 --> 00:27:50.263
and you have no honor.

00:27:50.297 --> 00:27:56.031
So tomorrow, you will kill me,
or I will kill you.

00:28:10.917 --> 00:28:13.385
Home two hours early?

00:28:13.420 --> 00:28:16.719
You better watch it.
I'll get used to this.

00:28:16.756 --> 00:28:18.883
Yep. They don't need me anymore.

00:28:18.925 --> 00:28:21.223
Home at 1700 every evening.

00:28:21.261 --> 00:28:24.594
You're such a bad liar.

00:28:27.934 --> 00:28:29.128
Hi!

00:28:29.169 --> 00:28:30.727
Hi.

00:28:30.770 --> 00:28:33.762
Sit down.
You look exhausted.

00:28:33.807 --> 00:28:35.399
Bad day?

00:28:37.844 --> 00:28:41.336
Miles, I think this woman
needs one of your famous

00:28:41.381 --> 00:28:42.439
neck massages.

00:28:42.482 --> 00:28:45.144
M-my hands are pretty cold.

00:28:45.185 --> 00:28:46.948
I'm not in the mood, anyway.

00:28:46.987 --> 00:28:49.547
Well, I can see the tension
in your muscles from here.

00:28:49.589 --> 00:28:50.556
No, thanks, really.

00:28:50.590 --> 00:28:53.821
Oh!
Um, I'm going to Bajor tomorrow.

00:28:53.860 --> 00:28:54.827
Just for a few days.

00:28:54.861 --> 00:28:56.453
- Bajor?
- Yes.

00:28:56.496 --> 00:28:58.464
I thought
I'd take the time and relax.

00:28:58.498 --> 00:29:00.864
A friend of mine has a house
in the Musilla Province.

00:29:00.900 --> 00:29:04.631
It's quiet, remote...
no distractions.

00:29:04.671 --> 00:29:06.571
Perfect!
When do you leave?

00:29:06.606 --> 00:29:08.801
Uh, first thing in the morning.

00:29:08.842 --> 00:29:11.003
W-W-Wait a minute.

00:29:11.044 --> 00:29:12.773
You can't go alone.

00:29:12.812 --> 00:29:15.246
What if you go into labor?

00:29:15.281 --> 00:29:16.339
Well, Julian doesn't think

00:29:16.383 --> 00:29:17.850
that's going to happen
for another month.

00:29:17.884 --> 00:29:19.545
But he doesn't know for sure.

00:29:19.586 --> 00:29:21.383
Miles...

00:29:21.421 --> 00:29:23.150
maybe you should go with her.

00:29:23.189 --> 00:29:24.156
What?

00:29:24.190 --> 00:29:25.384
I can't go.

00:29:25.425 --> 00:29:28.053
I have a botanical pathology
seminar tomorrow

00:29:28.094 --> 00:29:29.925
but you said yourself
things are slow in Ops.

00:29:30.030 --> 00:29:31.930
I don't think
that's a good idea.

00:29:31.998 --> 00:29:33.124
Me neither.

00:29:33.166 --> 00:29:35.896
Miles Edward O'Brien,
are you going to let

00:29:35.935 --> 00:29:38.426
the woman carrying
your unborn child

00:29:38.471 --> 00:29:40.439
go on a trip all by herself?

00:29:44.444 --> 00:29:46.571
Are you two fighting again?

00:29:46.613 --> 00:29:47.580
No!

00:29:47.614 --> 00:29:48.603
Not at all.

00:29:48.648 --> 00:29:49.945
Good.
Then it's settled.

00:29:50.016 --> 00:29:52.109
Miles, let's pack your bag.

00:30:02.696 --> 00:30:04.926
What if I just do what I did

00:30:04.964 --> 00:30:08.422
the last time a Klingon
wanted to kill me?

00:30:08.468 --> 00:30:10.095
I...

00:30:10.136 --> 00:30:13.765
throw my sword away,
kneel down in front of him

00:30:13.807 --> 00:30:16.435
and dare him to execute me.

00:30:16.476 --> 00:30:17.443
Yeah.

00:30:17.477 --> 00:30:18.501
He'll be humiliated

00:30:18.545 --> 00:30:21.480
and slink away
like a scalded targ.

00:30:21.514 --> 00:30:24.244
The only reason that worked
was because Gowron stepped in

00:30:24.284 --> 00:30:25.251
and restrained your opponent

00:30:25.285 --> 00:30:26.718
before he was able
to kill you.

00:30:26.753 --> 00:30:28.345
No one will stop Thopok.

00:30:28.388 --> 00:30:30.288
Dax and I aren't even
able to attend.

00:30:30.323 --> 00:30:33.622
So my choices are to not show up

00:30:33.660 --> 00:30:36.151
be branded a coward
and lose Grilka

00:30:36.196 --> 00:30:37.163
or die?

00:30:37.197 --> 00:30:38.164
Yes.

00:30:38.198 --> 00:30:39.290
Oh, come on now!

00:30:39.332 --> 00:30:40.993
There must be another way
out of this!

00:30:41.101 --> 00:30:44.229
You people have
rituals for everything

00:30:44.270 --> 00:30:45.897
except waste extraction.

00:30:45.939 --> 00:30:49.170
You must have a ceremony
or a secret handshake

00:30:49.209 --> 00:30:51.074
or something I can do?

00:30:57.150 --> 00:30:59.812
I have an idea.

00:31:18.972 --> 00:31:21.941
Oh, congratulations.

00:31:21.975 --> 00:31:24.273
How do you feel?

00:31:24.310 --> 00:31:25.937
Like a puppet...

00:31:25.979 --> 00:31:28.379
and I have some complaints
for the puppeteer.

00:31:28.414 --> 00:31:30.814
You nearly wrenched my arm
out of its socket.

00:31:30.850 --> 00:31:31.976
The movement
would not have hurt

00:31:32.085 --> 00:31:33.677
if you were in better
physical condition.

00:31:33.720 --> 00:31:36.621
Exercise makes me sweat.

00:31:36.656 --> 00:31:38.954
You need to get some sleep.

00:31:40.860 --> 00:31:42.953
If your body's tired tomorrow

00:31:42.996 --> 00:31:44.520
Worf won't even
be able to save you.

00:31:45.532 --> 00:31:46.499
Bedtime.

00:31:46.533 --> 00:31:47.522
Mm-hmm.

00:31:49.601 --> 00:31:53.128
I cannot believe the lengths
I'm going to for that Ferengi.

00:31:53.171 --> 00:31:55.639
I'm practically
giving him Grilka.

00:31:55.674 --> 00:31:59.303
What is it you see in her,
anyway?

00:31:59.344 --> 00:32:02.905
I mean, she's attractive,
but other than that?

00:32:02.948 --> 00:32:05.849
It is everything about her...

00:32:05.884 --> 00:32:10.048
the way she carries herself,
confident and strong.

00:32:10.088 --> 00:32:12.955
She commands those around her.

00:32:13.024 --> 00:32:14.753
The proud tilt of her head...

00:32:14.793 --> 00:32:17.694
the way her face betrays
none of her true feelings...

00:32:17.729 --> 00:32:20.289
the power of her voice.

00:32:20.332 --> 00:32:24.860
And her eyes... as hard
as separ gemstones

00:32:24.903 --> 00:32:26.894
and twice as sharp.

00:32:26.938 --> 00:32:29.498
Sounds like you're
describing a statue.

00:32:29.541 --> 00:32:31.975
What would you do
with a woman like that...

00:32:32.077 --> 00:32:35.240
put her up on a pedestal
and clean her every week?

00:32:35.280 --> 00:32:37.305
You do not understand.

00:32:37.349 --> 00:32:38.714
If I were in your shoes

00:32:38.750 --> 00:32:42.709
I would be looking for someone
a little more entertaining

00:32:42.754 --> 00:32:45.120
a little more fun

00:32:45.156 --> 00:32:49.923
and maybe even
a little more attainable.

00:32:49.961 --> 00:32:52.657
You are not in my shoes.

00:32:52.697 --> 00:32:53.857
Too bad.

00:32:53.899 --> 00:32:55.764
You'd be amazed at what I can do

00:32:55.800 --> 00:32:58.268
in a pair of size 18 boots.

00:33:16.888 --> 00:33:18.822
He's in position.

00:33:21.560 --> 00:33:25.189
Quark, son of Keldar,
why are you here?

00:33:25.230 --> 00:33:28.757
To... to ans...

00:33:34.806 --> 00:33:37.070
To answer the challenge
of Thopok

00:33:37.108 --> 00:33:38.700
to prove my honor...

00:33:40.145 --> 00:33:43.842
and to win the favor
of the Lady Grilka.

00:33:49.387 --> 00:33:53.881
The challenge has been given
and accepted.

00:33:53.925 --> 00:33:56.689
Let no one interfere!

00:33:58.096 --> 00:34:00.155
Mok!

00:34:28.059 --> 00:34:30.619
Where did you learn to
fight with a bat'leth?

00:34:30.662 --> 00:34:33.392
I'm a man of many talents.

00:35:06.131 --> 00:35:07.098
No!

00:35:07.132 --> 00:35:08.497
Wait!

00:35:08.533 --> 00:35:10.433
You damaged the optronic relay.

00:35:10.468 --> 00:35:11.867
Can you repair it?

00:35:11.903 --> 00:35:14.337
I don't know.

00:35:14.372 --> 00:35:15.464
Well?!

00:35:15.507 --> 00:35:19.773
I claim
the Right of... Proclamation.

00:35:21.913 --> 00:35:25.178
I've never heard
of the "Right of Proclamation."

00:35:25.216 --> 00:35:26.205
It is a Ferengi custom.

00:35:26.251 --> 00:35:28.116
Then it has no place here!

00:35:28.153 --> 00:35:29.677
I beg to differ!

00:35:29.721 --> 00:35:32.747
I am as proud of my heritage
as your are of yours

00:35:32.791 --> 00:35:34.588
and I will not be denied

00:35:34.626 --> 00:35:36.491
the opportunity
to express myself

00:35:36.528 --> 00:35:39.656
according to Ferengi custom.

00:35:39.698 --> 00:35:43.293
He has shown respect
to our traditions.

00:35:43.334 --> 00:35:46.326
We will do the same.

00:35:48.940 --> 00:35:50.430
What do you need to do?

00:35:50.475 --> 00:35:55.139
I must... make a speech.

00:35:55.180 --> 00:35:56.704
About what?

00:35:56.748 --> 00:35:58.773
About you.

00:35:58.817 --> 00:36:00.944
Get on with it!

00:36:00.985 --> 00:36:05.615
I do not know how,
but he is still alive.

00:36:05.657 --> 00:36:07.181
You must work faster.

00:36:07.225 --> 00:36:09.193
I'm going as fast as I can.

00:36:09.227 --> 00:36:12.924
Uh...

00:36:12.964 --> 00:36:16.058
to this end...
my blade soars...

00:36:16.101 --> 00:36:17.830
through the...

00:36:17.869 --> 00:36:20.599
aquarium of my soul

00:36:20.638 --> 00:36:24.130
seeking the kelp of discontent

00:36:24.175 --> 00:36:28.737
which must be caught,
so that the rocky bottom of love

00:36:28.780 --> 00:36:31.874
lie in waiting with...

00:36:31.916 --> 00:36:34.043
fertile sand

00:36:34.085 --> 00:36:38.078
for the coming seed
of Grilka's affection

00:36:38.123 --> 00:36:44.426
and yet, does this explain
my need for her?

00:36:44.462 --> 00:36:46.123
No.

00:36:46.164 --> 00:36:49.964
It is like
a giant cave of emptiness

00:36:50.001 --> 00:36:54.938
waiting for the bats
of love to hang by...

00:36:59.010 --> 00:37:03.071
Well, I guess
that's enough talking.

00:37:04.816 --> 00:37:07.341
Now, back to the fighting.

00:37:07.385 --> 00:37:09.216
No showing off this time, Worf.

00:37:09.254 --> 00:37:10.687
Just get it over with.

00:37:10.722 --> 00:37:12.246
I was not showing off.

00:37:18.363 --> 00:37:20.297
End it!

00:37:20.331 --> 00:37:23.095
If you insist.

00:37:31.643 --> 00:37:34.339
Maybe not.

00:37:34.379 --> 00:37:36.108
Maybe...

00:37:36.147 --> 00:37:42.052
I'll just pick up
your sword and...

00:37:55.466 --> 00:37:57.400
Give it to you... I guess.

00:38:02.373 --> 00:38:05.308
Thopok, your honor
is satisfied.

00:38:05.343 --> 00:38:07.004
I return your weapon

00:38:07.045 --> 00:38:11.209
and discharge you from my House.

00:38:22.827 --> 00:38:24.089
My lady.

00:38:27.932 --> 00:38:31.800
Do-MACH ah chee ghos eh-PAGH?

00:38:47.252 --> 00:38:50.278
Congratulations.
You did it.

00:38:50.321 --> 00:38:53.757
What does she see
in that parasite?

00:38:53.791 --> 00:38:54.883
Who knows?

00:38:54.926 --> 00:38:56.951
But they're on
the same wavelength

00:38:56.995 --> 00:38:59.259
and at least Quark
can see an opportunity

00:38:59.297 --> 00:39:00.696
when it's standing
in front of him.

00:39:00.732 --> 00:39:03.132
He would have to be
blind not to see it.

00:39:06.437 --> 00:39:08.872
MoVas ah-kee rustak.

00:39:12.308 --> 00:39:14.674
Computer, bat'leth.

00:39:16.479 --> 00:39:19.573
MoVas ah-kee rustak.

00:39:22.485 --> 00:39:27.320
Kosh tomaH...
ehpaq kaVeir Lukara.

00:39:27.357 --> 00:39:30.622
Ish-tovee chuCH thling nuq?

00:39:34.964 --> 00:39:37.592
Meklo boH ka Mech.

00:39:37.634 --> 00:39:40.797
Te-doQ roos ka Mech-TOH.

00:39:45.875 --> 00:39:47.274
Ow!

00:39:58.655 --> 00:40:00.179
So I guess we're going.

00:40:00.223 --> 00:40:01.554
Looks like it.

00:40:08.331 --> 00:40:11.562
Tell me about this...
this house we're going to.

00:40:11.601 --> 00:40:16.334
It's a gorgeous
200-year-old cottage.

00:40:16.372 --> 00:40:17.703
It's filled with antiques

00:40:17.740 --> 00:40:20.231
sitting in the middle
of a deep, dark forest.

00:40:20.276 --> 00:40:23.302
It's got three fireplaces,
two balconies.

00:40:23.346 --> 00:40:24.574
I see.

00:40:24.614 --> 00:40:27.777
It's, uh, 20 kilometers
from the nearest neighbor

00:40:27.817 --> 00:40:29.182
30 to the nearest town.

00:40:29.218 --> 00:40:31.709
Why am I not surprised?

00:40:31.754 --> 00:40:33.153
It gets worse.

00:40:33.189 --> 00:40:35.316
There's a view.

00:40:35.358 --> 00:40:36.325
Of what?

00:40:36.359 --> 00:40:37.383
Of the Holana River.

00:40:37.427 --> 00:40:39.224
You can see it from every room
in the house

00:40:39.262 --> 00:40:41.924
and at night,
when the stars are out

00:40:41.965 --> 00:40:44.195
and you can only hear
rushing water

00:40:44.233 --> 00:40:48.192
it may be one of the most
romantic spots

00:40:48.237 --> 00:40:49.204
in all of Bajor.

00:40:49.238 --> 00:40:50.796
That's it.

00:40:50.840 --> 00:40:52.171
I'm not going.

00:40:52.208 --> 00:40:54.335
I don't care what Keiko says,
I'm not going.

00:40:54.377 --> 00:40:55.344
You go.

00:40:55.378 --> 00:40:56.743
I'll wait an hour

00:40:56.779 --> 00:40:58.576
and then I'll, I'll tell her
that you left without me.

00:40:58.614 --> 00:40:59.706
That there was
a miscommunication

00:40:59.749 --> 00:41:00.716
about the departure time.

00:41:00.750 --> 00:41:01.808
You think she'll buy it?

00:41:01.851 --> 00:41:02.818
She'll probably

00:41:02.852 --> 00:41:04.319
accuse us of having
another fight,

00:41:04.354 --> 00:41:05.946
of behaving like children,
but I can handle that.

00:41:06.022 --> 00:41:07.421
The important thing is

00:41:07.457 --> 00:41:10.221
that we don't go anywhere
near that place together.

00:41:10.259 --> 00:41:12.557
You are absolutely right.

00:41:12.595 --> 00:41:15.155
In fact, I'm going
to go to the capital

00:41:15.198 --> 00:41:16.631
and see Shakaar.

00:41:16.666 --> 00:41:19.601
That's the best idea
you've had all week.

00:41:24.474 --> 00:41:25.600
Have a good trip.

00:41:25.641 --> 00:41:27.268
Thanks.

00:41:31.314 --> 00:41:33.111
It would've been nice.

00:41:34.617 --> 00:41:36.380
In another life.

00:41:37.854 --> 00:41:38.912
Let's not even think
about it.

00:41:38.955 --> 00:41:40.855
All right.
Let's not.

00:41:44.293 --> 00:41:45.783
Miles...?

00:41:45.828 --> 00:41:47.728
Yes, Nerys?

00:41:48.765 --> 00:41:50.460
Get out.

00:41:50.500 --> 00:41:53.230
Right.

00:41:57.740 --> 00:42:00.300
A compound fracture
of the right radius

00:42:00.343 --> 00:42:02.937
two fractured ribs,
torn ligaments

00:42:03.046 --> 00:42:05.947
strained tendons,
numerous contusions

00:42:06.049 --> 00:42:07.482
bruises and scratches.

00:42:07.517 --> 00:42:09.382
What have you been doing?

00:42:09.419 --> 00:42:13.515
You mean,
what have we been doing?

00:42:16.826 --> 00:42:18.919
Never mind.

00:42:18.961 --> 00:42:21.327
I don't need
that particular image

00:42:21.364 --> 00:42:23.059
running around my head.

00:42:23.099 --> 00:42:24.566
I'll just treat you.

00:42:26.836 --> 00:42:28.463
What happened to you two?

00:42:30.506 --> 00:42:31.803
We, um...

00:42:31.841 --> 00:42:35.368
Well, um, if you must know...

00:42:35.411 --> 00:42:36.571
No!

00:42:36.612 --> 00:42:40.844
No, uh...
I don't need that image either.

00:42:40.883 --> 00:42:43.147
In fact, I'm going to stop
asking that question altogether.

00:42:43.186 --> 00:42:45.154
People can come in,
I will treat them

00:42:45.188 --> 00:42:47.179
and that's all.

00:42:47.223 --> 00:42:49.817
Please... have a seat.

00:42:49.859 --> 00:42:51.884
I'll be with you in a minute.

00:43:12.315 --> 00:43:13.509
You do realize

00:43:13.549 --> 00:43:15.073
that according
to Klingon tradition...

00:43:15.118 --> 00:43:18.087
According to tradition,
we have to get married.

00:43:18.121 --> 00:43:21.955
But as you keep insisting,
you are not a traditional woman.

00:43:23.860 --> 00:43:26.158
The truth is, Worf

00:43:26.195 --> 00:43:31.326
at heart, you're not
much of a traditional man.

00:43:34.103 --> 00:43:36.435
You might be right.

00:43:36.472 --> 00:43:38.997
How do you wish to proceed?

00:43:40.676 --> 00:43:42.371
I don't know.

00:43:42.411 --> 00:43:44.072
You must have some idea.

00:43:44.113 --> 00:43:45.978
You were the...

00:43:46.015 --> 00:43:47.107
Aggressor?

00:43:47.150 --> 00:43:48.310
Yes.

00:43:48.351 --> 00:43:51.013
And now there are questions
that must be answered.

00:43:56.025 --> 00:43:57.219
Mmm.

00:43:57.260 --> 00:43:59.956
I don't feel like
answering questions.

00:43:59.996 --> 00:44:04.228
Why don't we just take it
one day at a time

00:44:04.267 --> 00:44:05.757
and see what happens?

00:44:10.806 --> 00:44:13.900
I, uh, do not like
the uncertainty

00:44:13.943 --> 00:44:15.433
of that arrangement.

00:44:17.580 --> 00:44:19.741
One thing's for certain...

00:44:19.782 --> 00:44:23.047
you've stopped thinking
about Grilka.
